---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

// Kit form 'labs-landing' — numeric form ID from its raw HTML embed
// (action="https://app.kit.com/forms/9705434/subscriptions"). This is
// distinct from the data-uid ("b56b520835") used by Kit's JS embed/styling.
const KIT_FORM_ID = '9705434';
const KIT_FORM_ACTION = `https://app.kit.com/forms/${KIT_FORM_ID}/subscriptions`;

// Kit form 'Labs Feedback' — created 2026-08-15 (data-uid 3a646885a2).
// Custom field 'labs_feedback_reason' (id 1339845) captures the selected
// reason directly from this page's raw POST; nothing in Kit's own form
// builder needs to match it.
const FEEDBACK_FORM_ID = '9806596';
const FEEDBACK_FORM_ACTION = `https://app.kit.com/forms/${FEEDBACK_FORM_ID}/subscriptions`;

// Single source of truth for the Lab schedule — the hero kicker, the
// Upcoming Sessions table, and the bottom CTA reminder all read from this
// so the dates/topics can't drift out of sync.
const SESSIONS = [
  {
    number: 1,
    topic: 'Identity',
    date: 'Friday, August 28, 2026',
    time: '8:00am PT / 11:00am ET',
    status: 'Registration open',
  },
  {
    number: 2,
    topic: 'Inner Knowing',
    date: 'Friday, September 25, 2026',
    time: '8:00am PT / 11:00am ET',
    status: null,
  },
  { number: 3, topic: 'Discomfort', date: 'October 2026', time: null, status: null },
  { number: 4, topic: 'Visibility', date: 'November 2026', time: null, status: null },
];
// Bump to SESSIONS[1] after Lab #1 runs (Aug 28) so the hero, the bottom CTA,
// and the feedback heading all roll forward to Inner Knowing. Lab #2 also needs
// its own Zoom link + LAB2 entry in lib/lab-schedule.ts before thank-you.astro
// can hand out a working calendar invite.
const nextSession = SESSIONS[0];
---
<Base
  title="Leadership Labs — Free Live Sessions for Introverted Leaders | Greg Weinger"
  description="A free monthly live session for introverted leaders. Bring your real challenges — we work through them together. Hosted by Greg Weinger of The Introverted Leader podcast."
  minimalHeader
>
  <section class="labs-hero">
    <p class="masterclass-kicker">Free Live Sessions</p>
    <h1>The Leadership Labs</h1>
    <figure class="masterclass-still">
      <img src="/masterclass-still.webp" alt="Greg Weinger" width="1200" height="676" />
    </figure>
    <div class="labs-hero-card">
      <p class="labs-session-label">Lab #{nextSession.number} — {nextSession.topic}</p>
      <p class="labs-date-badge">{nextSession.date} · {nextSession.time}</p>
      <p class="lead">Undoing the belief that who you are is the problem. Bring a real situation — we work through it together, live.</p>
      <form class="contact-form labs-hero-form" method="post" action={KIT_FORM_ACTION} id="signup">
        <div class="form-field">
          <label for="email_address">Email address</label>
          <input type="email" id="email_address" name="email_address" required placeholder="you@example.com" />
        </div>
        <button type="submit" class="btn-primary contact-submit">Save my spot →</button>
      </form>
    </div>
    <p class="labs-feedback-hint"><a href="#feedback">Can't make it? Tell me why →</a></p>
  </section>

  <div class="container">

    <section>
      <h2 class="home-section-label">The Four Topics</h2>
      <p>Identity is the first of four things that hold introverted leaders back — the Labs work through all of them over time.</p>
      <div class="card-grid">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Identity</h3>
          <p>Undoing the programming you've received that who you are is the problem. Until this shifts, tactics don't stick. We start here.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Inner Knowing</h3>
          <p>Learning to trust your intuitive read on a room, a person, a situation. Introverts are wired for this — and trained to ignore it. But you can tap in again.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Discomfort</h3>
          <p>Using anxiety, friction, and uncertainty as fuel instead of brakes. The capacity to sit with discomfort is a strength.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Visibility</h3>
          <p>Being seen in the moments that matter, without performing. If you've watched the masterclass, this is the deep-dive.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="home-section-label">Upcoming Sessions</h2>
      <div class="labs-table-wrap">
        <table class="labs-sessions-table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Lab</th>
              <th>Topic</th>
              <th>Date</th>
              <th>Status</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {SESSIONS.map((session) => (
              <tr>
                <td>#{session.number}</td>
                <td>{session.topic}</td>
                <td>{session.date}{session.time ? ` — ${session.time}` : ''}</td>
                <td>{session.status ?? '—'}</td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>Missed one? Every session is recorded. Sign up below and you'll get the recordings along with your invitation to the next live session.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="home-section-label">How It Works</h2>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Sign up</strong> — one email field, that's it.</li>
        <li><strong>Get your invitation</strong> — I'll send the link and calendar invite for the next live session.</li>
        <li><strong>Bring something real</strong> — a situation you're actually in. The Labs run on real cases, not hypotheticals.</li>
        <li><strong>Can't make it live?</strong> The recording lands in your inbox.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="contact-form-section labs-bottom-cta">
      <h2 class="home-section-label">Join the next free Lab</h2>
      <p class="labs-next-reminder">Next Lab: {nextSession.topic} — {nextSession.date}.</p>
      <a class="btn-primary contact-submit" href="#signup">Save my spot →</a>
    </section>

    <section id="feedback" class="contact-form-section labs-feedback-section">
      <h2 class="home-section-label">Can't make Lab #1?</h2>
      <p class="labs-next-reminder">Takes 10 seconds — it helps me plan future sessions.</p>
      <form class="contact-form labs-feedback-form" method="post" action={FEEDBACK_FORM_ACTION}>
        <fieldset class="labs-feedback-reasons">
          <legend>Why not?</legend>
          <label><input type="radio" name="fields[labs_feedback_reason]" value="Topic doesn't interest me" required /> The topic doesn't interest me</label>
          <label><input type="radio" name="fields[labs_feedback_reason]" value="Time doesn't work" /> The time doesn't work for me</label>
          <label><input type="radio" name="fields[labs_feedback_reason]" value="Prefer recording" /> I'd rather watch the recording than attend live</label>
          <label><input type="radio" name="fields[labs_feedback_reason]" value="Not for me right now" /> Just not for me right now</label>
          <label><input type="radio" id="reason-other" name="fields[labs_feedback_reason]" value="Other" /> Something else</label>
          <div class="labs-feedback-other-detail">
            <label for="reason-other-text">Tell me more (optional)</label>
            <input type="text" id="reason-other-text" name="fields[labs_feedback_other]" placeholder="What would make this a yes?" />
          </div>
        </fieldset>
        <div class="form-field">
          <label for="feedback_email">Email address</label>
          <input type="email" id="feedback_email" name="email_address" required placeholder="you@example.com" />
        </div>
        <button type="submit" class="btn-primary contact-submit">Send feedback</button>
      </form>
    </section>

    <section class="about-teaser">
      <img class="about-teaser-img" src="/greg-weinger.webp" alt="Greg Weinger" width="80" height="80" />
      <div>
        <h2 class="home-section-label">About Your Host</h2>
        <p>I'm Greg Weinger. I spent over 25 years rising to the executive level of software companies as an introvert — most of those years in denial about it. For the past two years I've been interviewing the most effective introverted leaders and experts I could find on <strong>The Introverted Leader</strong> podcast — people who got promoted, built influence, and advanced without becoming someone they weren't. The Labs are where those patterns get applied to your situation, live.</p>
        <p>New here? Start with the free masterclass — <em>Why Everything You've Been Told About Getting Ahead as an Introvert Is Wrong.</em> <a href="/masterclass">Watch it free →</a></p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <p class="pull-quote">You're not behind. You're just running a different play.</p>

  </div>
</Base>
